{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dba4a475-f5d4-4227-bdd7-4ae39dd7e6bb","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3. WebFetch/WebSearch allowed (≤10 calls) for multiecuscan.net's published per-model function lists (Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia 2.0T: modules, parameters, actuators, adjustments/procedures, coding) and MES's help/manual; also read the local install read-only: C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MultiEcuScan (help files, Modules/vehicle lists, any readable .txt/.ini/.html; the database is encrypted — do not try to decrypt). Minimal repo grepping. Report under 150 words. Others own owner_*/m_*, fullscan/liveboard/scan_health/scanlog, system_detail/system.html, dossier MIL, mes analysis/catalog/cuore_log, experience_*: do not edit; you own NEW docs/research/MES_VS_CUORE_CAPABILITY_2026-10-14.md, NEW mes-log-mcp/mes/mes_functions.py (knowledge table), NEW cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py, NEW cuore/web/templates/_mes_handoff.html + one include line in tests.html and job.html step 6 (additive; re-read before editing), cuore/api/tests.py (additive route), cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py. You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nOwner's question: what can MES access/modify/service better than CUORE; review and compare, then add or improve. Do:\n1. Capability matrix (the doc): rows = every function class MES offers on this platform (all-module scan incl. IHS/CH via A5/A6 cables, module info/identity, per-module live parameters with names/units/scaling, graphs/recording to CSV, freeze frames per module, actuator tests, adjustments/procedures — service interval reset, battery/BMS registration, EPB service mode, ABS bleed, steering angle sensor calibration, throttle/idle learn, injector/coil coding, DPF/regens n/a, proxi alignment/config, key/RF functions, TPMS write, etc. — list only what the sources show for Giulia/Stelvio, each with the module and a source URL/date), columns = MES (yes/no + notes), CUORE today (yes/partial/no with the module/file), gap, and the safe way to close it: (a) read-side → implement in CUORE when a sourced DID/PID exists, else \"needs DID definition (TechAuthority / learn)\"; (b) write-side (routines, adjustments, coding) → CUORE never performs them from HTTP; MCP-only with consent for the few catalogued actuators; for the rest, a **MES handoff card**. Be explicit where MES is better (parameter scaling for TCM/BCM/ABS, adjustments, coding, cable guidance) and where CUORE is better (verdict/evidence gate, Mode 06 interpretation, cross-session history, hypotheses, reports, mobile, honesty labels).\n2. mes_functions.py: the matrix as data (function id, module, kind read|actuator|adjustment|coding, MES menu path as documented, prerequisites, what to record afterwards, source, confidence).\n3. MES handoff cards: on the Tests page and Job step 6, for any catalogue test or fault-tree step whose action is something MES does and CUORE does not (ESIM actuator, battery registration, service reset, EPB service mode, ABS bleed, SAS calibration): a card \"Do this in MES: <module> → <menu path>; before: <prereqs, cable colour, MES not holding the port warning>; after: record the result here\" with a result form that stores an attested test/service record (reuse checklists.set_result / service ledger) and, when MES wrote a CSV recording or log, a \"Import the MES log/recording\" button that points the mes catalog at the new file (the catalog already rescans) and links it to the record. Handoff never writes to the car.\n4. Improve what CUORE can do better than MES right now, in this pass, small: on import of an MES SCAN/FES log, auto-create the scan entry in the Scans timeline (source MES) and run the health report over it so an MES session gets the same report a CUORE scan gets (use scanlog/scan_health public functions; do not edit their files — call them).\nTests: matrix table loads with ≥25 functions each with a source; handoff card renders for esim_commanded_vent_test with the MES path and prerequisites; recording a result stores it; importing a copied SCAN_2610080920.txt into a temp MES root yields a Scans entry with source MES and a health report line. Run check_mes_handoff.py, check_tests_page.py, check_jobs_page.py, check_screens.py. Commit \"MES vs CUORE capability matrix; MES handoff cards; MES logs get the same scan entry and health report\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"fe6b9595-e1bf-46d2-8336-f0c52308599f","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:03:34.357Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
