{"parentUuid":"c9636dfa-770f-4215-b79f-1d4187c2cee3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WTxyFyLfUPkY4iPnpBD7kb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio battery registration BMS adjustment procedure\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Giulia/Stelvio BCM adjustment for \\\"Race Mode\\\" - Multiecuscan\",\"url\":\"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7707\"},{\"title\":\"Battery replacement.\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/battery-replacement.1190455/\"},{\"title\":\"MultiEcuScan question regarding IBS\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/multiecuscan-question-regarding-ibs.1214903/\"},{\"title\":\"New MultiEcuScan 4.6\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/new-multiecuscan-4-6.1190364/\"},{\"title\":\"2018 Alfa Giulia - Proxi Alignment issue` - Multiecuscan\",\"url\":\"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7784\"},{\"title\":\"MultiECUscan Use, Tips and Issues\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/multiecuscan-use-tips-and-issues.40594/page-3\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan (MES) - Popular Settings Compilation - Electronics - Giulia Tech Community\",\"url\":\"https://giuliatech.com/t/multiecuscan-mes-popular-settings-compilation/80\"},{\"title\":\"What are PROXI parameters for AGM battery on Giulia 2.2\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/what-are-proxi-parameters-for-agm-battery-on-giulia-2-2.65519/page-3\"},{\"title\":\"MultiECUscan - Squadra Tuning\",\"url\":\"https://squadra-tuning.com/obd-tools/multiecuscan/\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan - Diagnostics software for Italian cars\",\"url\":\"https://www.multiecuscan.net/supportedvehicleslist.aspx\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about MultiEcuScan battery registration procedures for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Battery Type Registration via MultiEcuScan\n\nBattery type configuration is found in the Body → CAN Setup section, specifically in byte 63, bits 5 (or bits 0-3 in some documentation). Different battery types are configured with specific bit patterns, including 80Ah 680A (xxxx0001), 95Ah 800A (xxxx0010), H7 flooded (xxxx1000), H7 AGM (xxxx1001), H8 flooded (xxxx1010), and H8 AGM (xxxx1011).\n\n## PROXI Alignment Procedure\n\nThe PROXI Alignment procedure in MultiEcuScan involves writing CAN configuration data to multiple modules, including the Body Computer Node (BCM/NBC) and Engine Control Node (ECM/NCM).\n\n## BMS-Related Limitations\n\nFor 2020 onwards Giulia's and Stelvio's, the IBS (Intelligent Battery Sensor) interface has changed for some parameters. IBS Battery Charge Status is the parameter that can be trusted, though later model Giulia's have limited IBS parameter support in MultiEcuScan.\n\nFor the most detailed and current procedure information, I recommend consulting the official MultiEcuScan manual or community forums dedicated to Giulia/Stelvio modifications, as these settings can vary based on model year and regional specifications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"618f8309-1508-4d63-ba35-c18be127020c","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:31.634Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio battery registration BMS adjustment procedure","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TTup9ejmaQpMhCG2D2tw19","content":[{"title":"Giulia/Stelvio BCM adjustment for \"Race Mode\" - Multiecuscan","url":"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7707"},{"title":"Battery replacement.","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/battery-replacement.1190455/"},{"title":"MultiEcuScan question regarding IBS","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/multiecuscan-question-regarding-ibs.1214903/"},{"title":"New MultiEcuScan 4.6","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/new-multiecuscan-4-6.1190364/"},{"title":"2018 Alfa Giulia - Proxi Alignment issue` - Multiecuscan","url":"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7784"},{"title":"MultiECUscan Use, Tips and Issues","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/multiecuscan-use-tips-and-issues.40594/page-3"},{"title":"Multiecuscan (MES) - Popular Settings Compilation - Electronics - Giulia Tech Community","url":"https://giuliatech.com/t/multiecuscan-mes-popular-settings-compilation/80"},{"title":"What are PROXI parameters for AGM battery on Giulia 2.2","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/what-are-proxi-parameters-for-agm-battery-on-giulia-2-2.65519/page-3"},{"title":"MultiECUscan - Squadra Tuning","url":"https://squadra-tuning.com/obd-tools/multiecuscan/"},{"title":"Multiecuscan - Diagnostics software for Italian cars","url":"https://www.multiecuscan.net/supportedvehicleslist.aspx"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about MultiEcuScan battery registration procedures for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## Battery Type Registration via MultiEcuScan\n\nBattery type configuration is found in the Body → CAN Setup section, specifically in byte 63, bits 5 (or bits 0-3 in some documentation). Different battery types are configured with specific bit patterns, including 80Ah 680A (xxxx0001), 95Ah 800A (xxxx0010), H7 flooded (xxxx1000), H7 AGM (xxxx1001), H8 flooded (xxxx1010), and H8 AGM (xxxx1011).\n\n## PROXI Alignment Procedure\n\nThe PROXI Alignment procedure in MultiEcuScan involves writing CAN configuration data to multiple modules, including the Body Computer Node (BCM/NBC) and Engine Control Node (ECM/NCM).\n\n## BMS-Related Limitations\n\nFor 2020 onwards Giulia's and Stelvio's, the IBS (Intelligent Battery Sensor) interface has changed for some parameters. IBS Battery Charge Status is the parameter that can be trusted, though later model Giulia's have limited IBS parameter support in MultiEcuScan.\n\nFor the most detailed and current procedure information, I recommend consulting the official MultiEcuScan manual or community forums dedicated to Giulia/Stelvio modifications, as these settings can vary based on model year and regional specifications."],"durationSeconds":6.794239200115204,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a74feed-c41b-4654-b65b-336408ea7f0b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c9636dfa-770f-4215-b79f-1d4187c2cee3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"de848150-5d7d-4fc8-a21e-36f8fd5f7e30","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011iYVGUJn7aVhGGzzVYKRY8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio service interval reset oil change adjustment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"displayed oil change interval on menu->service\",\"url\":\"https://www.fiatforum.com/threads/displayed-oil-change-interval-on-menu-service.504582/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Reset service light .\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-service-light.59696/\"},{\"title\":\"How to reset oil info with multiecuscan\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-oil-info-with-multiecuscan.51691/\"},{\"title\":\"DIY Oil Changes ?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/diy-oil-changes.7601/\"},{\"title\":\"MultiECUScan reset issue\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/multiecuscan-reset-issue.54793/\"},{\"title\":\"Oil Change and Service Reset using MultiEcuScan\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/oil-change-and-service-reset-using-multiecuscan.705170/\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan Help\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/multiecuscan-help.19957/\"},{\"title\":\"Scheduled Maintenance Reset\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/scheduled-maintenance-reset.24621/\"},{\"title\":\"MES & Oil Change routines\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/mes-oil-change-routines.24067/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about using MultiEcuScan for Giulia and Stelvio service interval and oil change resets:\n\n## Oil Change Reset\n\nFor the Giulia, the oil change reset is found in Engine > Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0) > Adjustments > Oil Change. After an oil change, you need to reset it in two places - under Service and then in the engine ECU oil-change.\n\n## Service Interval Reset\n\nThe service interval reset is in Service > Service Interval Reset > Adjustments > NEXT SERVICE KM RESET. You can change the service interval to your desired distance.\n\n## Important Considerations for Newer Models\n\nOn newer models like Giulia and Stelvio, it is not possible to write higher values for service intervals. \n\nFor cars with a Security Gateway (SGW), you need an SGW bypass to successfully execute resets. Alfa added a Security Gateway in later models blocking the ability to write to the OBD port.\n\nWhen the coupon number is \"0,\" you can't set service intervals - only an oil reset in the engine is possible.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5eaa933c-8580-4874-9267-a3d141deb2cb","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:31.845Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio service interval reset oil change adjustment","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01R7M1nHPwvry3UVdrUwatYR","content":[{"title":"displayed oil change interval on menu->service","url":"https://www.fiatforum.com/threads/displayed-oil-change-interval-on-menu-service.504582/"},{"title":"How to Reset service light .","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-service-light.59696/"},{"title":"How to reset oil info with multiecuscan","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-oil-info-with-multiecuscan.51691/"},{"title":"DIY Oil Changes ?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/diy-oil-changes.7601/"},{"title":"MultiECUScan reset issue","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/multiecuscan-reset-issue.54793/"},{"title":"Oil Change and Service Reset using MultiEcuScan","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/oil-change-and-service-reset-using-multiecuscan.705170/"},{"title":"Multiecuscan Help","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/multiecuscan-help.19957/"},{"title":"Scheduled Maintenance Reset","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/scheduled-maintenance-reset.24621/"},{"title":"MES & Oil Change routines","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/mes-oil-change-routines.24067/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about using MultiEcuScan for Giulia and Stelvio service interval and oil change resets:\n\n## Oil Change Reset\n\nFor the Giulia, the oil change reset is found in Engine > Magneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0) > Adjustments > Oil Change. After an oil change, you need to reset it in two places - under Service and then in the engine ECU oil-change.\n\n## Service Interval Reset\n\nThe service interval reset is in Service > Service Interval Reset > Adjustments > NEXT SERVICE KM RESET. You can change the service interval to your desired distance.\n\n## Important Considerations for Newer Models\n\nOn newer models like Giulia and Stelvio, it is not possible to write higher values for service intervals. \n\nFor cars with a Security Gateway (SGW), you need an SGW bypass to successfully execute resets. Alfa added a Security Gateway in later models blocking the ability to write to the OBD port.\n\nWhen the coupon number is \"0,\" you can't set service intervals - only an oil reset in the engine is possible."],"durationSeconds":6.257708899974823,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a74feed-c41b-4654-b65b-336408ea7f0b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"de848150-5d7d-4fc8-a21e-36f8fd5f7e30","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"350cfe14-f795-4f58-a105-9cd08d9687f1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JEprdfnLma4YpNYWumoyEZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio EPB electric parking brake service mode pad replacement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Brake pad replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-pad-replacement.47740/\"},{\"title\":\"Brakes stuck in service mode!\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/brakes-stuck-in-service-mode.20545/\"},{\"title\":\"2017-2019 Giulia & Stelvio Parking Brake Switch: Failure, Warnings & Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/parking-brake-kit-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2024\"},{\"title\":\"Brake Service Mode within MultiEcuScan Software\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-service-mode-within-multiecuscan-software.54344/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Put the Electronic Parking Brake into Service Mode on a Alfa Romeo Stelvio (2017–present)\",\"url\":\"https://servicereset.net/maintenance/alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-present-epb-service-mode/\"},{\"title\":\"Let's try to solve the brake pad swap -> car killing itself\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/lets-try-to-solve-the-brake-pad-swap-car-killing-itself.41506/\"},{\"title\":\"Rear Brake Pad Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/rear-brake-pad-replacement.22961/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Reset the EPB (Electronic Parking Brake) with an OBD2 Scanner Iamcarhacker\",\"url\":\"https://iamcarhacker.com/obd2-scanner/service-functions/how-to-reset-the-epb-electronic-parking-brake-with-an-obd2-scanner/\"},{\"title\":\"REPLACING REAR PADS ON ST\",\"url\":\"https://www.explorerst.org/threads/replacing-rear-pads-on-st.5985/\"},{\"title\":\"Problem with Electronic Parking Brake system\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/problem-with-electronic-parking-brake-system.53568/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about MultiEcuScan and EPB (electronic parking brake) service mode for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio pad replacement:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Service Mode Access:**\nYou do not need a special scan tool for brake service mode—it can be accessed through the vehicle's infotainment screen by navigating to Settings > Driver Assistance > Brake Service, and following the prompts to retract the electronic parking brake pistons.\n\n**MultiEcuScan's Role:**\nYou don't need MultiEcuScan for doing either the front or rear brake pad replacement. However, you will need MultiECU to reset the brake light after the work is complete.\n\n**EPB Maintenance Mode in MultiEcuScan:**\nThe EPB maintenance mode in MultiEcuScan doesn't work; all you need for a brake job is to go through the Infotainment.\n\n**Procedure Summary:**\nTo fit new rear pads you must wind the motors fully open first (called Brake Service Mode), and the good news is this mode lives in the infotainment system, so a routine rear pad change needs no wiTECH or generic OBD EPB tool.\n\nIn summary, for Giulia and Stelvio pad replacement, you primarily use the infotainment system for service mode, and MultiEcuScan is mainly needed afterward to clear diagnostic codes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"782964de-f6aa-481d-9af6-9cb5800bae29","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:09:32.264Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"MultiEcuScan Giulia Stelvio EPB electric parking brake service mode pad replacement","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012BiqcDaBcH1j9q6e6vgNmN","content":[{"title":"Brake pad replacement","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-pad-replacement.47740/"},{"title":"Brakes stuck in service mode!","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/brakes-stuck-in-service-mode.20545/"},{"title":"2017-2019 Giulia & Stelvio Parking Brake Switch: Failure, Warnings & Replacement","url":"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/parking-brake-kit-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2024"},{"title":"Brake Service Mode within MultiEcuScan Software","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-service-mode-within-multiecuscan-software.54344/"},{"title":"How to Put the Electronic Parking Brake into Service Mode on a Alfa Romeo Stelvio (2017–present)","url":"https://servicereset.net/maintenance/alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-present-epb-service-mode/"},{"title":"Let's try to solve the brake pad swap -> car killing itself","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/lets-try-to-solve-the-brake-pad-swap-car-killing-itself.41506/"},{"title":"Rear Brake Pad Replacement","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/rear-brake-pad-replacement.22961/"},{"title":"How to Reset the EPB (Electronic Parking Brake) with an OBD2 Scanner Iamcarhacker","url":"https://iamcarhacker.com/obd2-scanner/service-functions/how-to-reset-the-epb-electronic-parking-brake-with-an-obd2-scanner/"},{"title":"REPLACING REAR PADS ON ST","url":"https://www.explorerst.org/threads/replacing-rear-pads-on-st.5985/"},{"title":"Problem with Electronic Parking Brake system","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/problem-with-electronic-parking-brake-system.53568/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about MultiEcuScan and EPB (electronic parking brake) service mode for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio pad replacement:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Service Mode Access:**\nYou do not need a special scan tool for brake service mode—it can be accessed through the vehicle's infotainment screen by navigating to Settings > Driver Assistance > Brake Service, and following the prompts to retract the electronic parking brake pistons.\n\n**MultiEcuScan's Role:**\nYou don't need MultiEcuScan for doing either the front or rear brake pad replacement. However, you will need MultiECU to reset the brake light after the work is complete.\n\n**EPB Maintenance Mode in MultiEcuScan:**\nThe EPB maintenance mode in MultiEcuScan doesn't work; all you need for a brake job is to go through the Infotainment.\n\n**Procedure Summary:**\nTo fit new rear pads you must wind the motors fully open first (called Brake Service Mode), and the good news is this mode lives in the infotainment system, so a routine rear pad change needs no wiTECH or generic OBD EPB tool.\n\nIn summary, for Giulia and Stelvio pad replacement, you primarily use the infotainment system for service mode, and MultiEcuScan is mainly needed afterward to clear diagnostic codes."],"durationSeconds":7.034422800064087,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0a74feed-c41b-4654-b65b-336408ea7f0b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"350cfe14-f795-4f58-a105-9cd08d9687f1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
