{"parentUuid":"ad1d1a1d-34ba-4936-a880-5d4213d913c9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DzE2eWoA6VjYy1gNT4ZBU2","type":"tool_result","content":"14-Maserati VIN, ``ZN661XUA9JX000001`` (WMI ``ZN6`` -- Maserati North America;\n15-see ``mes.platform.marque_for_vin`` and ``cuore.services.shop_bridge.\n16-_WMI_MAKES``), with one synthetic clean FES log written into a throwaway\n17:``MES_LOG_DIR`` so this test is fully self-contained -- it does not touch\n18-the real MultiEcuScan install, and does not need the Stelvio's real corpus\n19-to be present. The log has no DTCs, so no sibling-platform case-memory\n20-cross-reference (``mes.experience``) has anything to surface for it; the\n21-\"no Stelvio/Alfa text\" checks below are therefore a plain substring\n22-search, not a case-memory-aware one -- there is nothing in this fixture's\n23-own history for that carve-out to need to apply to.\n24-\n25-Six checks:\n26-  1. ``GET /start`` (before any VIN is chosen) responds 200 and its own\n27-     copy is marque-neutral (\"Start this car\", not \"Start this Stelvio\" --\n--\n66-\n67-# --- the synthetic Maserati fixture -----------------------------------------\n68-#\n69:# MES_LOG_DIR must be set, and the log file written, before `cuore` (and\n70-# therefore `mes`) is imported -- mes.paths.configured_roots() reads the env\n71-# var once, lazily, but nothing here relies on that laziness, so the order\n72:# is kept strict and obvious. Pointing MES_LOG_DIR at a throwaway directory\n73-# (rather than appending to the real install) means this test sees ONLY the\n74-# Maserati fixture -- no real Stelvio data, no risk of the two corpora's\n75-# vehicles getting merged or this test accidentally passing because of\n76-# something the real corpus happened to contain.\n77-\n78-VIN = \"ZN661XUA9JX000001\"  # Maserati North America WMI (ZN6); synthetic fixture\n79-\n80-_LOG_DIR = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-marque-logs-\"))\n81-_FES_LOG = _LOG_DIR / \"FESLog_2610130900_Maserati Grecale.txt\"\n82-_FES_LOG.write_text(\n--\n98-    \"No fault codes\\n\",\n99-    encoding=\"utf-8\",\n100-)\n101:os.environ[\"MES_LOG_DIR\"] = str(_LOG_DIR)\n102-\n103-ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n104-sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fba259f9-fa57-4d05-b475-e491273cc442","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:10:37.942Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"14-Maserati VIN, ``ZN661XUA9JX000001`` (WMI ``ZN6`` -- Maserati North America;\n15-see ``mes.platform.marque_for_vin`` and ``cuore.services.shop_bridge.\n16-_WMI_MAKES``), with one synthetic clean FES log written into a throwaway\n17:``MES_LOG_DIR`` so this test is fully self-contained -- it does not touch\n18-the real MultiEcuScan install, and does not need the Stelvio's real corpus\n19-to be present. The log has no DTCs, so no sibling-platform case-memory\n20-cross-reference (``mes.experience``) has anything to surface for it; the\n21-\"no Stelvio/Alfa text\" checks below are therefore a plain substring\n22-search, not a case-memory-aware one -- there is nothing in this fixture's\n23-own history for that carve-out to need to apply to.\n24-\n25-Six checks:\n26-  1. ``GET /start`` (before any VIN is chosen) responds 200 and its own\n27-     copy is marque-neutral (\"Start this car\", not \"Start this Stelvio\" --\n--\n66-\n67-# --- the synthetic Maserati fixture -----------------------------------------\n68-#\n69:# MES_LOG_DIR must be set, and the log file written, before `cuore` (and\n70-# therefore `mes`) is imported -- mes.paths.configured_roots() reads the env\n71-# var once, lazily, but nothing here relies on that laziness, so the order\n72:# is kept strict and obvious. Pointing MES_LOG_DIR at a throwaway directory\n73-# (rather than appending to the real install) means this test sees ONLY the\n74-# Maserati fixture -- no real Stelvio data, no risk of the